{
  "name": "Formdall lead triage",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "54d99d14-c202-4eaf-a6f9-52f7925a7049",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -608,
        -368
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "## Formdall lead triage\n\n### How it works\n\nFormdall verifies the form submission and posts the lead to this webhook. An AI agent (Mistral) reads the message and scores it hot, warm, or junk. Hot leads post to Slack and get logged to Google Sheets. Warm leads get a Gmail draft reply for you to review. Junk leads stop at Ignore Lead Entry.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n1. Add a Header Auth credential to When Formdall Lead Received.\n2. Add your Mistral Cloud credential to Mistral AI Model.\n3. Connect Slack, Google Sheets, and Gmail credentials, or delete the branches you do not use.\n4. Replace YOUR_SHEET_ID in Append Lead to Sheets with your own spreadsheet, and #sales in Post Message to Slack with your channel.\n5. Publish the workflow and paste its production URL into your Formdall webhook action.\n\n### Requirements\n\nAn n8n instance reachable from the internet, a Formdall form with a webhook action, and a Mistral Cloud API key (swap in another chat model if you prefer).\n\n### Customization\n\nEdit the system prompt in Lead Analysis Agent to change what counts as hot, warm, or junk. Swap Mistral AI Model for any other chat model and keep the prompt and schema. Add outputs to Route by Lead Score for more scores.\n\nFull walkthrough: https://formdall.de/en/guides/n8n-lead-triage/"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "2ef5837f-45e7-4a0f-a26e-75aff615a2e1",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -48,
        -160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 432,
        "height": 320,
        "content": "## Receive and verify lead\n\nReceives the lead from Formdall. The signature check is optional and disabled by default; enable it only after setting FORMDALL_SIGNING_SECRET as described in the guide."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "408bd597-c5f5-42a3-9071-9cfbd675a133",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        416,
        -176
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 400,
        "height": 560,
        "content": "## Analyze lead with AI\n\nThe agent scores the lead hot, warm, or junk and returns score, category, summary, and reply_draft, enforced by the structured output parser."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "683164e9-29f3-4f93-abf5-5b0a46d37a86",
